From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ecm_interface: accelerate ports behind a qca-8021q switch

A port of a switch behind a firmware port has no firmware interface, so
ECM cannot accelerate it. With the qca-8021q tagging protocol the port
reaches its conduit as an 802.1Q VLAN, the port's own or the one of the
bridge it forwards in, and the tag is the same in both directions. Treat
such a port as that VLAN on top of the conduit, which the firmware
carries like any other VLAN, and take the egress priority map only from
real VLAN devices. The tag of such a port is always on the conduit, so
the bridge VLAN check of the rule builders takes it as tagged. In a
VLAN-aware bridge the port carries the bridge VLAN of the flow, that of
the VLAN device on the bridge or the bridge PVID, and that VLAN device
adds no tag of its own.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
